<title>USA: Deutsche Bank may issue $1.0 bln in debt. [CORRECTED 22:34 GMT]</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank may issue $1.0 bln in debt. [CORRECTED 22:34 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank is expected to issue a $1.0 billion yankee debt offering one day next week, syndicate sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to consist of an Aa1/AA-plus rated 10-year yankee issue with Deutsche Morgan Grenfell as lead underwriter for the offering, the sources added.</p>
<p>(Corrects rating from &quot;A1/AA-plus&quot; to &quot;Aa1/AA-plus&quot;.)</p>
<p>Dealers said unofficial price talk on Deutsche's yankee issue was seen in the low 50's (basis points) area.</p>
<p>--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675</p>
</text>
